<h1>
Deductive Reasoning in AI Agents: A Neuro-symbolic Planner for Green Retrofitting
</h1>

<p class="lead">
<h2>Abstract</h2>

Due to the limitations in humans’ bounded rationality, when consuming
information provided by AI models, epistemic risks are high (Bougzime et al., 2025; Nisa
et al., 2026). A neuro-symbolic system architecture is proposed to re-route the knowledge base
in AI agents back to human tacit knowledge and expertise rather than relying on historical data. 
To optimise green retrofitting project constraints, rules are hard coded by experts as the symbolic layer, as seen from the right-hand side of Figure 1.
The LLMs then leverage the neural efficiency with deductive reasoning in the rule-based system.
The main advantage of a neuro-symbolic structure is to reduce reliance on long retrieved text in documents by encoding
expert tacit knowledge as compact rules.

